module std.realization_reconcile

import std.types { String, Bool }

data realization_reconcile_doc: String = "Canonical reconcile-and-verify-ground carrier. SHARED substrate: runner-slot, PXE, and ctrl reconcile all import this; systemd-oomd is its FIRST instance, not its owner (home is std, the layer all consumers point toward). Signed-signature intent: reconcile_grounded(apply_effect, show_read, grounds_predicate) -> Converged { evidence } | NotConverged { reason }. The fn is named reconcile_GROUNDED (not bare reconcile) because the v1 seed interpreter binds a bare fn call by name across the WHOLE closure (flat namespace, fail-open by import order); three distinct reconcile concepts -- this verify-effective grounding, std.realization.reconcile (RealizedStep fold/dedup), and product.budget_tree.reconcile (node vs actual) -- co-occur in a single consumer closure (gunbc.fleet_host_budget imports all three transitively), so a bare reconcile call mis-dispatched (the grounding call hit the steps-fold body -> undefined variable steps) until this disambiguation. The flat fn namespace itself is the substrate root (operator-steered, DESIGN section 6); unique names are the documented seed remedy. SUBSTRATE DEVIATION (reported for sign-off): the v1 seed cannot type a fn-typed parameter whose return is a generic-applied enum (fn(R) -> Grounding<E> fails at the annotation), so grounds_predicate cannot be passed as a higher-order arg here. Closest faithful realization: reconcile takes the grounding VALUE (Grounding<E>, which a caller derives by applying its predicate to the observed read) and enforces the read-presence gate. DESIGN section 5 invariants kept: (1) a ReadAbsent show_read yields NotConverged regardless of the grounding passed, so evidence is structurally impossible without an OBSERVED read; (2) the verdict never depends on apply_effect (trusting the declaration-that-it-was-applied over the read would be fail-open), so apply_effect is threaded as provenance only. Residue the substrate cannot close (documented honestly, not hidden): the carrier cannot itself re-run the predicate over the observed value, so coupling the grounding to THAT read is the caller's obligation; the oomd instance discharges it with no hand-grounding seam by deriving the grounding from the matched read value inline."

data realization_reconcile_instance_contract_marker: String = "CALLER OBLIGATION (signed by bright-stag-194 2026-06-23; binds EVERY instance of this carrier: oomd today, PXE / runner-slot / ctrl reconcile next). Because the carrier cannot re-run the grounding predicate over the observed read value (v1-seed substrate limit, see realization_reconcile_doc), coupling the grounding to THAT read is the caller's duty. Every instance MUST: (a) derive the Grounding INLINE by matching over the OBSERVED read value and grounding the matched value -- never pass a pre-computed grounding decoupled from the read; (b) ship a DISCRIMINATING fail-open witness -- a perturbation that makes a non-grounding read produce evidence MUST flip the witness RED. This marker keeps the substrate residue honest and named (DESIGN section 6 named-residue; section 5 executable-witness backstop), not hidden. Reference instance and its witness: gunbc.oomd_install (ground_oomd_from_read derived inline in reconcile_oomd) + test.claim.oomd_install_grounding_witness (oomd_install_grounding_holds, perturb-RED proven)."

type ShowEffectiveRead<R>
  = ReadObserved { value: R }
  | ReadAbsent { reason: String }

type Grounding<E>
  = Grounds { evidence: E }
  | DoesNotGround { reason: String }

type Reconciliation<A, E>
  = Converged { evidence: E, applied: A }
  | NotConverged { reason: String, applied: A }

fn reconcile_grounded<A, R, E>(
  apply_effect: A,
  show_read: ShowEffectiveRead<R>,
  grounding: Grounding<E>
) -> Reconciliation<A, E> {
  match show_read {
    ReadAbsent { reason: why } => NotConverged { reason: why, applied: apply_effect }
    ReadObserved { value: _ } =>
      match grounding {
        Grounds { evidence: e } => Converged { evidence: e, applied: apply_effect }
        DoesNotGround { reason: why } => NotConverged { reason: why, applied: apply_effect }
      }
  }
}

fn reconciliation_converged<A, E>(r: Reconciliation<A, E>) -> Bool {
  match r {
    Converged { evidence: _, applied: _ } => true
    NotConverged { reason: _, applied: _ } => false
  }
}
